# Local development

Next.js 16 app. Default dev URL: http://localhost:3000

## First-time setup

```bash
npm install
```

Create `.env.local` with at least `DATABASE_URL` (Neon Postgres — same production database as [techxiv.dev](https://www.techxiv.dev); see `database.mdc`). Copy optional PostHog vars from `.env.example` if needed.

`postinstall` runs `prisma generate`; re-run after schema changes:

```bash
npm run db:generate
```

## Start the dev server

```bash
npm run dev
```

Next.js binds to port 3000 by default. Use a different port if 3000 is taken:

```bash
npm run dev -- -p 3002
```

Before starting, check for an existing process on the target port:

```bash
lsof -i :3000
```

Run the dev server in the background when starting it from an agent session.

## Production build (optional)

```bash
npm run build
npm start
```

`npm start` also defaults to port 3000.
